WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.558 --> 00:00:14.300
do you mean, the trolls got Gliss?"

2
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.500
Perda exclaimed.

3
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.102
Darb was breathing hard; he'd obviously run the whole way to the meeting spot.

4
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:25.183
"We landed by the riverbank, just like Zann told us to," he said.

5
00:00:25.203 --> 00:00:27.464
"At first we thought we were okay.

6
00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:32.871
Then some trolls appeared out of nowhere and grabbed Gliss before we realized they were even there.

7
00:00:33.932 --> 00:00:37.234
I tried to stop them, but they pushed me down and carried her away."

8
00:00:39.175 --> 00:00:41.517
Zann was too stunned to speak for a moment.

9
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:45.140
"This is all my fault," he blurted out at last.

10
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.002
"I told Gliss she'd be safe, and she believed me."

11
00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:52.204
"It's not your fault, Zann," Perda said.

12
00:00:52.224 --> 00:00:54.286
"We all knew we were taking a risk."

13
00:00:55.066 --> 00:00:57.148
"We need to rescue her," Zann said.

14
00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:01.167
"We have to go to the zoo and find the wild dragon pen."

15
00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.088
Perda shook her head.

16
00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:05.790
"Sounds like a great way to get all of us captured.

17
00:01:06.431 --> 00:01:10.414
We need to stick to our plan and find the Magic Masters you've been telling us about.

18
00:01:11.155 --> 00:01:14.017
They might have some ideas about how to rescue Gliss."

19
00:01:14.858 --> 00:01:17.160
For a second Zann wanted to argue.

20
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.623
He knew that Gliss must be terrified, and he wanted to rescue her if he could.

21
00:01:22.604 --> 00:01:24.525
But he also knew that Perda was right.

22
00:01:25.186 --> 00:01:27.568
Rushing to the zoo would only get them all captured.

23
00:01:27.852 --> 00:01:28.572
They needed help.

24
00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:30.533
"Okay," he said.

25
00:01:30.553 --> 00:01:33.514
"One of Boz's friends lives really close to here.

26
00:01:34.295 --> 00:01:35.315
Let's try him first.

27
00:01:35.755 --> 00:01:36.215
Follow me."

28
00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.677
Zann led his friends to a house a few blocks away.

29
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:42.658
When he knocked, a young woman opened the door.

30
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:45.579
Her eyes looked red, as if she'd been crying.

31
00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:49.301
"Yes?" she said, sounding suspicious.

32
00:01:49.681 --> 00:01:50.521
"What do you want?"

33
00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:53.382
"Uh, hello," Zann said.

34
00:01:53.402 --> 00:01:55.103
"We're looking for Lonz.

35
00:01:55.803 --> 00:01:56.844
Does he still live here?

36
00:01:57.672 --> 00:02:03.694
He's an old friend of my grandfather's, and His voice trailed off as the young woman started sobbing.

37
00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.954
She hid her face in her hands.

38
00:02:10.476 --> 00:02:11.456
is my father.

39
00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:14.297
He was one of the first Reds they took!"

40
00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:16.938
she said, her words muffled and sad.

41
00:02:17.718 --> 00:02:18.898
Zann's heart sank.

42
00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.879
"I'm sorry," he said.

43
00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:23.279
"My grandfather was taken too.

44
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.780
I'm really sorry."

45
00:02:27.908 --> 00:02:28.449
"Now what?"

46
00:02:28.749 --> 00:02:30.830
Darb asked a moment later as they walked away.

47
00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.533
"Do you think Morb already captured all of Boz's friends?"

48
00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.196
"I hope not," Perda said, sounding worried.

49
00:02:38.916 --> 00:02:41.078
Zann tried not to think about that possibility.

50
00:02:41.098 --> 00:02:45.541
"Boz's friend Saffa lives right across the river from here," he said.

51
00:02:45.561 --> 00:02:47.642
"Let's try her house next."

52
00:02:48.303 --> 00:02:51.225
They walked as quickly as they could, watching out for trolls.

53
00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:55.268
Every time they saw one, they ducked into a doorway or behind a tree.

54
00:02:56.908 --> 00:03:02.032
Finally they reached a neighborhood of brightly colored homes with small but tidy front yards.

55
00:03:02.832 --> 00:03:06.034
Zann had to stop to think about which one belonged to Boz's friend.

56
00:03:06.054 --> 00:03:10.217
"I wish we could check the Directory for the address," he said.

57
00:03:10.898 --> 00:03:11.598
Perda frowned.

58
00:03:11.618 --> 00:03:13.319
"Too risky," she said.

59
00:03:13.339 --> 00:03:15.541
"Just try to remember."

60
00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.862
"I'm pretty sure it's that one."

61
00:03:18.623 --> 00:03:20.484
Zann led his friends to a nearby house.

62
00:03:21.225 --> 00:03:23.546
Taking a deep breath, he knocked on the door.

63
00:03:24.827 --> 00:03:26.148
A middle-aged man answered.

64
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.661
"Yes, can I help you?"

65
00:03:28.061 --> 00:03:29.382
he asked in a weary voice.

66
00:03:30.202 --> 00:03:32.303
"I'm looking for Saffa," Zann said.

67
00:03:32.323 --> 00:03:33.844
"Is this the right house?"

68
00:03:34.685 --> 00:03:36.106
The man's face crumpled.

69
00:03:36.126 --> 00:03:38.947
"Yes. But my wife isn't here anymore.

70
00:03:39.688 --> 00:03:41.749
The trolls came for her the day before yesterday.

71
00:03:42.509 --> 00:03:45.251
Saffa tried to zap away, but she wasn't fast enough."

72
00:03:45.971 --> 00:03:48.132
"We're sorry to bother you," Perda said.

73
00:03:48.152 --> 00:03:50.374
"I hope she comes back soon."

74
00:03:51.394 --> 00:03:54.016
Perda, Zann, and Darb returned to the street.

75
00:03:54.884 --> 00:03:57.325
"Maybe this isn't such a good idea," Darb said.

76
00:03:57.345 --> 00:04:00.986
"You said these people are all famous Magic Masters, right?

77
00:04:01.706 --> 00:04:04.907
Morb might be keeping an eye on their houses to try to catch their friends."

78
00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:06.407
Perda gulped.

79
00:04:06.728 --> 00:04:07.368
"Or us."

80
00:04:07.388 --> 00:04:10.069
"Maybe," Zann said.

81
00:04:10.089 --> 00:04:14.630
"But we have to save Gliss, and I don't know how we can do that on our own.

82
00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.551
Besides we haven't tried going to Teplo's house yet.

83
00:04:19.311 --> 00:04:21.672
If anyone could hide from Morb, it's him.

84
00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.603
Boz always said that Teplo was the most creative magician he ever knew."

85
00:04:26.623 --> 00:04:28.845
"Really?" Perda said.

86
00:04:28.865 --> 00:04:30.005
"What's he like?"

87
00:04:30.025 --> 00:04:32.767
"I never met him," Zann admitted.

88
00:04:32.787 --> 00:04:38.852
"He was away studying the nomads on the Far Frontier the whole time I lived in First City.

89
00:04:39.572 --> 00:04:43.375
But Boz has told me all kinds of cool stories about him."

90
00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:46.137
"Okay, let's go find him," Darb said.

91
00:04:46.957 --> 00:04:47.998
Perda nodded grimly.

92
00:04:48.018 --> 00:04:50.740
"And let's hope Morb didn't find him first."

93
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.542
Soon they reached a house that looked different from any of the other homes on the block.

94
00:04:56.543 --> 00:05:02.166
It was tall and narrow, with oddly shaped windows and a statue of a gangly bird atop the

95
00:05:02.206 --> 00:05:02.847
pointy roof.

96
00:05:02.867 --> 00:05:05.548
"Are you sure this is the right place?"

97
00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.089
Darb sounded dubious.

98
00:05:07.109 --> 00:05:10.651
"Yes. Boz pointed it out to me a few times."

99
00:05:11.491 --> 00:05:16.174
Taking a deep breath, Zann walked up the steep front steps to the wooden porch.

100
00:05:16.955 --> 00:05:19.176
He signaled for Perda and Darb to follow him.

101
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.303
Zann hoped the porch might hide them if any trolls wandered by.

102
00:05:24.103 --> 00:05:25.004
He knocked on the door.

103
00:05:25.404 --> 00:05:28.847
A young woman with black hair and an intelligent expression answered.

104
00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.009
"Hi," Zann said.

105
00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:32.690
"We're looking for Teplo.

106
00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:33.711
Is he here?"

107
00:05:34.472 --> 00:05:35.633
The young woman shook her head.

108
00:05:35.653 --> 00:05:38.975
"Sorry. He's gone, just like the rest of the Reds in town."

109
00:05:39.696 --> 00:05:41.557
The young woman closed the door in his face.

110
00:05:41.577 --> 00:05:47.402
"I can't believe Morb already captured all the Magic Masters," Perda exclaimed.

111
00:05:47.422 --> 00:05:49.724
"I can," Darb replied.

112
00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.421
"He captured Boz, didn't he?"

113
00:05:52.121 --> 00:05:54.542
Zann shrugged, opening his mouth to answer.

114
00:05:55.223 --> 00:05:59.525
But before he could say a word, he felt the porch floor shudder beneath his feet.

115
00:06:00.325 --> 00:06:06.128
A second later a trapdoor fell open, sending all three kids tumbling down into total darkness.
